\frac{9}{10} = \frac{9 \times 3}{10 \times 3} = \frac{27}{30}
\] \[
\frac{5}{6} = \frac{5 \times 5}{6 \times 5} = \frac{25}{30}
\] Now we can add the fractions. \[
\frac{9}{10} + \frac{5}{6} = \frac{27}{30} + \frac{25}{30} = \frac{27 + 25}{30} = \frac{52}{30}
\] Next, we need to simplify the fraction \(\frac{52}{30}\). The greatest common divisor of 52 and 30 is 2. Dividing the numerator and the denominator by 2, we get \[
\frac{52 \div 2}{30 \div 2} = \frac{26}{15}
\] So, the answer is \(\frac{26}{15}\). </think> <answer> \(\frac{26}{15}\) </answer>

